<div class="wrap">

  <!-- ══════════ PREFACE ══════════ -->
  <section class="preface">
    <div class="preface-body">
      <p>The Reader is informed that this little almanack contains twenty-five limericks, all of them concerning persons named <b>Bill</b>, and none of them flattering — there being no rhyme in "flattering," and the Editors being on good terms with none of the limericks. Among our Bills one will find a butcher, a banker, a busker, and one very dangerous <em>economist</em> from the Strand; one will meet a Herr <em>Jurgen</em>, who is owing somebody a <em>bill</em>; and one will be reminded, over and over, that the <em>bill</em> at a public house is the one limerick we never quite get over.</p>
      <p>Each verse is annotated in the margin by the undersigned, who asks for nothing in return but a glass, and who denies nothing — including the parrot. Where a Bill of record appears in the accompanying plates, it is shown with the kind of licence the engraver's art allows. Drink these verses slowly, aloud, and preferably standing.</p>
      <p class="sig">— The Editor, who insists is not one of the Bills (but is owed a bill)</p>
